body:
Headless hands-on drive (real viewport picks through `interact::pick_at`, the real form widgets, Cmd+Z/Cmd+Y): all 7 steps pass, covering 3-2-1, offset, undo, move-the-fixture, degenerate picks, interpenetration and staleness. It found one real bug, fixed in 8a11b1ec:
- **Stock (95f3d4f3):** locating a turned part also turned a square box stock by the part's full rotation, so it tilted and sank 17 mm into the vise floor, and the Face op faced air. Now a stock square to the setup keeps its orientation and is refitted around the part's new place with each side's allowance kept (`stock_follow.rs`). A pure translation is unchanged. The interpenetration warning now also names a stock sinking into the fixture. Plain Model-page `MoveModel` keeps today's rigid follow and will get its own follow-up issue.
- **UI (8a11b1ec):**
  - mates read in plain words ("part face -Z (bottom), #1 on vise face +Z (top), #2");
  - a refused draft shows "Not yet: <why>" instead of offering Apply;
  - the offset frame and the turn's positive sense are labelled;
  - a hint says to hide the fixture when a buried part face is wanted.
- **Tests:** `fixture_locate_stock` (3, each failed before), `stock_follow` units, and ui `locate_tests` (readable mates; a refused draft says why), plus `fixture_rows` and `structural` updates.
- **Gate:** the fixture, align, stock and undo suites pass; clippy is clean.
